<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet  xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>More Implicit Curves</title>
<p>
  In the equation <m>x^{3}-y^{3}=18 x y</m>, <m>y</m> is an implicitly
  function of <m>x</m> (except at <m>(0,0)</m>). The graph of
  <m>x^{3}-y^{3}=18 x y</m> is shown in <xref ref="fig_cubic_implicit"/>.
</p>
<figure xml:id="fig_cubic_implicit" >
        <caption>An Implicit Curve</caption>
        <image width="50%">
                <description>
                        <p>
                                        A grid from -12 to 12 in each direction with the graph of the curve defined by <m>x^{3}-y^{3}=18xy</m>, with points at negative nine comma nine, negative four comma eight, and negative eight comma four, as well as tangent lines to the curve at each of the points.
                        </p>
                </description>
                <xi:include href="./CubicImplicit.xml"/>
        </image>
</figure>
<exercise>
        <statement>
                <p>
        Verify that <m>(-9,9)</m>, <m>(-4,8)</m>, and <m>(-8,4)</m> are on the curve.
                </p>
        </statement>
</exercise>
<exercise>
        <statement>
                <p>
                        Calculate the derivative of <m>y</m> implicitly. That is, find <m>\frac{\di{y}}{\di{x}}</m> for the curve.
                </p>
        </statement>
</exercise>
<exercise>
        <statement>
                <p>
                        Find the equations of the tangent lines to the curve for each of the three given points.
                </p>
        </statement>
</exercise>
<exercise>
        <statement>
                <p>
                                Find the points where the tangent line at <m>(-9,9)</m> intersects each of the other two tangent lines.
                </p>
        </statement>
</exercise>
<exercise>
        <statement>
                <p>
                        Find the coordinates of any points where there is a horizontal tangent line.
                </p>
        </statement>
</exercise>
<exercise>
        <statement>
                <p>
                        Find the coordinates of any points where there is a vertical tangent line.
                </p>
        </statement>
</exercise>
<exercise>
        <statement>
                <p>
                        For points on the curve near the point <m>(-9,9)</m>, estimate the value of <m>y</m> for <m>x=-8.9</m>.
                </p>
        </statement>
</exercise>
</worksheet>
